/* This file is run through "gcc -E -P -x c" before it is packed into the
 * /etc romfs (nuttx/cmake/nuttx_toolchain.cmake:92), so comments have to be
 * C comments - a '#' line is an invalid preprocessing directive and fails
 * the build. The upside is that these comments never reach the board.
 *
 * Two rules for anything added below:
 *
 * 1. Keep lines under 64 characters. NSH reads a script line with
 *    readline_fd(buffer, CONFIG_NSH_LINELEN, ...) and CONFIG_NSH_LINELEN is
 *    64 here, so the tail of a longer line comes back as the next line and
 *    is parsed as a command of its own.
 *
 * 2. Do not run anything that can fail. nsh_initscript() leaves
 *    NSH_PFLAG_IGNORE clear, so apps/nshlib/nsh_script.c loops
 *    "while (ret >= 0)" and the first failing command silently drops every
 *    line below it. This script used to start with "audio_setup", which is
 *    not a builtin in any config in this tree, so every boot printed
 *    "nsh: audio_setup: command not found" and stopped there - bluetoothd
 *    and ai_agent never ran at all.
 *
 * /data/misc/bt holds the bond database (service/common/bt_storage.c) and the
 * last-NAP address that PAN auto-reconnect reads back on the next boot
 * (profiles/pan/panu_service.c). bluetoothd creates it itself:
 * create_bt_folder() in service/src/btservice.c mkdir()s /data/misc and
 * /data/misc/bt and treats EEXIST as success. So this script must not.
 * "mkdir -p /data/misc/bt" here broke rule 2 on every boot after the first -
 * apps/nshlib/nsh_fscmds.c cmd_mkdir returns the raw mkdir() result, and with
 * -p an existing final component only suppresses the error *message*, still
 * handing -1 back to NSH, which then dropped the three lines below.
 *
 * This script used to "rm -rf /data/misc/bt" right here, which threw away
 * the bond database and last_nap on every boot: the phone had to be paired
 * again after each reset, and PAN auto-reconnect had no address to aim at.
 */
bluetoothd &
sleep 2
ai_agent -d &
